From: Denys Vitali <denys@denv.it>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: omap4: espresso: reserve secure-world RAM

The stock espresso kernel removes the SMC (3 MiB at 0xbfd00000) and the
secure-input heap (14 MiB at 0xbef00000) from memblock. Mainline maps
them as RAM; under memory pressure this produces imprecise external
aborts (SIGBUS in userspace). Reproduced with stress-ng; see
pmos-galaxy docs/bringup.md.
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi	2026-11-03 12:03:46.923277668 +0000
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi	2026-11-03 12:03:48.187259288 +0000
@@ -20,6 +20,21 @@
 			reg = <0xbef00000 (1024 * 600 * 4)>;
 			no-map;
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * Stock (Samsung/TI) kernels memblock_remove() the top 17 MiB of RAM:
+		 * the secure-input ION heap (tiler1d, 14 MiB) and the secure monitor
+		 * (SMC, 3 MiB). Linux touching them raises imprecise external aborts.
+		 */
+		secure_input: secure-input@bef00000 {
+			reg = <0xbef00000 0xe00000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		smc: smc@bfd00000 {
+			reg = <0xbfd00000 0x300000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
 	};
 
 	chosen {
